A||||3||Leadfoot||Supercharge kit.......pros and cons||||1||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||07-10-2001||03:41 PM||||Does anyone know if there is a supercharger kit available for the fiero?  I have been looking around I can't seem to find a site.  I was about to contact Eaton, but want to know if anyone here has the info.?  Also, what are the pros and cons of such kits (if any exist)?  My buddy says that a supercharger is better since you don't have turbo lag, but I thought that this isn't really an issue.  The thing I like about the superchargers is that you don't have to mess with the cooling system, oil system and exhaust system or install an intercooler.  I saw a kit for my jeep and it claimed a 30-50 hp boost, 3 seconds off 0-60 and an installation time of 4-6 hours.  I wonder how much of that is smoke and mirrors?  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||07-10-2001||03:50 PM||||The Fiero Shop in Canada sells a supercharger<BR>kit. I heard there was some bugs with the old compressor that they used but that they've since switched to a Vortech brand.<BR>Here's their web-site: <A HREF="http://www.thefieroshop.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefieroshop.com</A> <P>You do have to mess with the oil and cooling system when installing a supercharger though.<P>As for turbo lag: this has been practically eliminated with modern turbos and isn't as big a problem with a light torquey car like the Fiero anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||07-10-2001||05:40 PM||||Hey Foot!<BR>How deep are your pockets?<BR>To turbo or super charge an engine that isn't built for it involves a lot of block, crank, piston and rod work...<BR>It is not a bolt on propasition...<BR>Unless you like to see large puddles of oil filled with the bottom end of your engine...<P>If you do have the resources, then by all means, go for it!<BR>I love hearing the whine of a blower on a street car!<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||07-10-2001||05:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierowrecker:<BR><B>Hey Foot!<BR>How deep are your pockets?<BR>To turbo or super charge an engine that isn't built for it involves a lot of block, crank, piston and rod work...<BR>It is not a bolt on propasition...<BR>Unless you like to see large puddles of oil filled with the bottom end of your engine...<P>If you do have the resources, then by all means, go for it!<BR>I love hearing the whine of a blower on a street car!<BR>crash...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Doesn't Design 1 sell a plug and play turbo kit?  I thought if they have a plug-in kit for a turbo why not a supercharger?  Man, I got to stop watching road warrior.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
